data.content:
Fixed and verified. Summary:

**`docs/index.md`** — wrapped `accessible <span class="platform ...">` in a `<span class="platform-line">` so the pair is treated as one unit:
```
text: Create beautiful,<br/><span class="platform-line">accessible <span class="platform web">web</span></span><br/>apps.
```

**`docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css`** — added:
```css
.platform-line {
  white-space: nowrap;
}

@media (max-width: 639px) {
  .platform-line {
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
}
```

Verified in the browser across viewport widths with every platform label (including the longest, "WordPress"):
- Desktop/tablet (≥640px): plenty of room, no wrap, unchanged size.
- Common phones (375–390px): fits with 25–50px to spare after the 0.85em shrink.
- Very old/narrow devices (320px, e.g. 1st-gen iPhone SE): still slightly tight (~15–25px overflow) even shrunk — flagging this as a known edge case for a device width that's largely obsolete now; let me know if you want it hardened further (e.g., wrapping allowed only below 360px, or a shorter "WP" label).

